tant is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "template_override": 1}, {"id": 11, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn8le09ob07re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nWrite a dialogue encouraging a colleague through a difficult situation!\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Controlling the Story", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Confronting Farmani", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe rules and obligations through a wider range of language and expressions in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Managing a Delicate Meeting", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When a business crisis arises, people may worry and begin to lose their confidence in the situation, in themselves, or each other. Meetings must be handled delicately to avoid relationship breakdown.  Delicate wording of your questions and assumptions is important.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A way to handle such delicate situations is to show confidence in your business partner or employee. Assume the best about people, give hope, and show that you believe in them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "1. Assuming the best = you don't really know but you want to believe they are making good decisions and doing good work.<br><span class=\"italic\">Examples<br><ul><li>I understand that you have written up the report?</li><li>I believe that you've spoken with Ryan?</li><li>Although this wasn't your fault ... the last shipment arrived too late.</li></ul> </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2. Giving Hope = point out what is positive in any situation. When things are looking good, mention it, and when things are looking really bad, find something to make it not seem so discouraging.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Examples<br><ul><li>Robert's latest assignment may lead to an answer.</li><li>There is hope that the new government may turn things around.</li><li>At least we won't need to worry about losing the other shares. (a bad situation)</li><li>We might quickly see some returns in the other investment. (a good situation)</li></ul> </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\"> Assuming the Best</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\"> Giving Hope</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I believe you have ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" ... may lead to a solution/an answer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I understand that you have ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" There is hope that ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Although this wasn't/isn't your fault ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You won't have to worry about ... (something bad)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Although the situation was beyond your control ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" At least ... (something bad) ... won't happen.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I believe you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You may soon ... (something good)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I'm sure of that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" We might quickly ... (something good)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When presenting information, we often need to quantify. Background information is usually unspecific. It is not the time to present the details of exact figures and amounts, but we must give some indication for a general idea of the situation. We do this by using quantifiers of general amounts.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use certain quantities with <span class=\"italic\">count nouns</span>  and others for <span class=\"italic\">non-count nouns</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For instance, <span class=\"italic\">work</span>  is not a <span class=\"italic\">count noun</span>. It is never used in the plural. However, tasks and assignments are countable. Therefore, to indicate that your business partner has done a small amount of work, you may say:<br><span class=\"italic\">He has done <span class=\"underline\">little</span> work.</span> <br> (or using the negative)<br><span class=\"italic\">He has <span class=\"underline\">not</span>  done <span class=\"underline\">much</span> work</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "But tasks, jobs and assignments are specific. They are count nouns so you may say:<br><span class=\"italic\">He has done <span class=\"underline\">few</span> jobs</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">He has <span class=\"underline\">not</span>  done <span class=\"underline\">many</span>  assignments</span> .", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":6,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Extreme\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Small Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Neither large nor small Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Large Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Extreme\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"count\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not ...<br> any ...<br> none of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a few (of) ...<br/> not many ...<br/> not that many ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"some ...<br/> several ...<br/> various ...<br/> a fair number of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"many ...<br/> a great ...  <br/> numerous ...<br/> plenty of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"all of ...<br/> all ...<br/> each of ...<br/> each ...<br/> every one of ...<br/> every ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" non-count\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nothing ... <br> no ...<br/> none (of)  ... <br> not ...<br/> (verb) ...<br/>any ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"few ...<br/>   a little ...<br/> a bit of ... <br> not much of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"some (of) ...<br/> a fair bit of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"plenty of ... <br/> much ...<br> a lot of ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"all ...<br/> all of ...<br/>   everything ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">None of</span> our clients arrived. (count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">None of</span> our staff arrived.  (non-count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">A few of</span> our clients are late. (count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Not much of</span> our staff is late. (non-count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">A fair bit of</span> our country was hit by tornadoes. ( non-count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">A fair number of</span> our provinces were hit by tornadoes. (count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Many employees</span> on strike. (count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Much of the staff</span> is on strike. (non-count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll do <span class=\"underline\">each of</span> the assignments. (count)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll do <span class=\"underline\">all</span> the work. (non-count)", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bring forward ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to present or introduce something to be seen, heard or discussed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I understand you have looked into the issue I brought forward yesterday?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear when holding a meeting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "keep behind one's back", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep something secret while pretending things are different", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"cont